==Spanish==

===Etymology===
Perhaps from {{etyl|de|es}} {{m|de|Gott|bei Gott|by God}}, because, when taking an [[oath]], some men, once they said "by God", aimed at the superior lip with the [[index finger]], [[symbolising]] forming the [[cross]] with the fingers and kissing it. Compare Portuguese ''[[bigode]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/bi.ˈɣo.te/|lang=es}}

===Noun===
{{es-noun|m}}

# [[moustache]], [[mustache]]; [[moustaches]], [[mustaches]]
# [[whisker]], [[whiskers]]

====Usage notes====
May be used in the singular or plural with the same meaning, as in English.

